            T("In atomic physics the **electronvolt** (eV) is the convenient unit: $1\\ \\text{eV} = 1.60 \\times 10^{-19}$ J. A useful shortcut for photon energy is $E\\ (\\text{eV}) = \\dfrac{1240}{\\lambda\\ (\\text{nm})}$, which comes from $hc = 1.24 \\times 10^{-6}$ eV m (a rounded value)."),
            H("Stopping potential"),
